A (before): `...emptyAfterPartial,\n  );\n});` — expect(...) closes with `);` then `});` ends the test.
B (after dart format): `...emptyAfterPartial,\n  );\n},\n);` — hmm, that reads `},\n);` — a trailing comma inside??

Wait: `);},);` — that's `);` `}` `,` `)`. That looks like dart format turned
```dart
    expect(
      classifyEmptyCompletion(turn, turn.last as AssistantMessage),
      EmptyCompletionVerdict.emptyAfterPartial,
    );
  });
```
into
```dart
    expect(
      classifyEmptyCompletion(turn, turn.last as AssistantMessage),
      EmptyCompletionVerdict.emptyAfterPartial,
    );
  },
  );
```
?? That's bizarre. `},\n);` would be a trailing comma after `}` then `)` — valid Dart? `test(..., () { ... }, );` — yes! A trailing comma after the LAST argument. dart format 8.x with "tall style" (the new formatter in Dart 3.7+) reformats trailing commas differently!

AH — THAT's it. The project was formatted with the OLD dart style (before Dart 3.7 tall-style), or with a different format config. The Dart SDK here is 3.13.5 whose formatter applies tall style; the committed code is in the OLD style (e.g. `dart format` from SDK < 3.7). Running today's `dart format` REWRITES large parts of the repo into tall style.

Check: does the repo pin a format style? Many files — if I format these 3 files with the new style, they'd diverge stylistically from the rest of the repo (which was formatted with the same SDK though?). Hmm wait — CI uses `dart-lang/setup-dart@v1 sdk: stable` = 3.13.x too. If the repo files were old-style, CI doesn't run a format gate (we found none), so no CI failure. The pre-commit hook? Let me check .git/hooks or the pre-commit script.

Actually — WAIT. More careful: `);});` vs `);},);` — hold on, B has `},\n);` — but there was no trailing comma in A at that point (`});`). Tall style ADDS trailing commas when args span lines. So yes — tall-style rewrite.

The real question: is the WHOLE REPO old-style (in which case formatting just these 3 files creates inconsistency), or are these 3 files merely hand-edited post-format (in which case formatting them restores consistency)?

Test: run `dart format --output=none --set-exit-if-changed` on a sample of UNCHANGED repo files (e.g. lib/src/agent/agent_loop.dart, lib/src/cli/agent_cli.dart — which ARE in the changed set but were formatted by previous passes...). Better: pick files NOT in the PR, e.g. lib/src/agent/misuse_breaker.dart, test/cli/hep_test.dart.

